## Why this unit exists

Root activation appended the five scoped successors onto the current lock. `tools/verify_design.py` requires contract parent **paths sorted and unique**. All five historical records list inventory v10 after an m1/m2 successor (`m2/...` then `m1/repository...`, or `rust-provider...` then `repository...`). That is unsorted. Independent check: each of the five `successor.json` parent arrays fails `paths == sorted(set(paths))`. Their pins, reviews, and assents still match `evidence/prior-unit-evidence.json` and **must not be selected**.

The failed five-unit lock (15 contract successors) was run through the **unmodified** verifier against this product: `Design verification failed: contract parents paths must be sorted and unique`. The current product lock still has **8 inventory + 10 contract** successors and **does** verify (`passed: true`, `productQualification: false`). No verifier weakening. No manufactured assent.

